## Deliverable 4: Menu Structure Examples\
\
### 1. Independent Restaurant (Global Casual Dining)\
- **Menu:** Dinner Menu\
- **Categories:** Starters (Soups, Salads), Mains (Pasta, Seafood, Meat), Sides, Desserts, Beverages (Wine, Soft Drinks).\
- *Note:* Standard hierarchical flow, moderate customisation.\
\
### 2. East African Local-Food Restaurant (Kenya/Tanzania)\
- **Menu:** Traditional Swahili & Local Menu\
- **Categories:** \
  - *Snacks & Street Food* (Samosa, Mandazi, Rolex)\
  - *Mains* (Nyama Choma, Chicken Pilau, Fish Curry)\
  - *Foundation Staples* (Ugali, Wali wa nazi, Chapati) *[Mapped to C003]*\
  - *Fresh Accompaniments* (Kachumbari, Sukuma Wiki)\
  - *Beverages* (Chai, Kahawa, Fresh Passion Juice, Sodas)\
- *Note:* Elevates staples to their own category, reflecting cultural dining patterns rather than forcing them into "Sides".\
\
### 3. Multi-Location Caf\'e9 Chain\
- **Menu Collection:** All-Day Menu, Breakfast Menu (06:00\'9611:00)\
- **Categories:** Hot Coffee (Espresso, Filter), Cold Coffee, Traditional Tea, Pastries & Bakes, Light Mains (Sandwiches, Salads).\
- *Multi-location feature:* "Avocado Toast" item exists in the central master. Location A (City Centre) prices it at $8.50; Location B (Suburb) prices it at $7.50. Both share the same `ItemID`.\
\
### 4. Hotel with Several Service Points\
- **Menu Collection:** Room Service Menu, Pool Bar Menu, Fine Dining Restaurant Menu.\
- **Structure:** \
  - *Room Service:* Combos/Bundles (Club Sandwich + Fries + Soda), simplified categories for ease of ordering.\
  - *Fine Dining:* \'c0 la carte, highly detailed subcategories (e.g., "From the Raw Bar", "Dry-Aged Steaks").\
- *Note:* Same underlying kitchen items (e.g., "Grilled Chicken") are repackaged into different menus with different markups and presentations.\
\
### 5. Bakery / Confectionery\
- **Menu:** Daily Bake Menu\
- **Categories:** Artisan Breads (Sourdough, Baguettes), Viennoiserie (Croissants, Danishes), Cakes (Whole, By the Slice), Biscuits & Cookies, Beverages (Coffee, Tea).\
- *Note:* Classification driven by production method and shelf-life rather than meal course.\
\
### 6. Bar / Beverage-Focused Venue\
